IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `prt-payroll`
IMPORT `prt-qa`

-- Pay-roll Tax Assessment Act 2002 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (prt-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role
-- and every situation.
--
-- Both roles are employers (s 4), so 25 of the 27 questions arise for both, and are asked for both. The two of the
-- employment agent (ss 4, 9GA) are asked for the employer with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed
-- term"). Each question that takes the situation input, `the kind of employer I am`, is asked with each value under
-- which it does not arise, every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the employer (the baseline's
-- seat) each question's answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. The agent's
-- answers are worked by hand from the text; mirror cases ask the same facts from both seats.
--
-- Facts: Daniel's d044 (1 June 2031) and the baseline's other fixtures, copied from prt-cases-payroll.l4 (a case file
-- cannot be imported without running its assertions); the salaries are the baseline's ASSUMPTIONS. Cases marked FORMULA
-- rest on formulas the deposited text drops (../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_42096.formulas.md). Expected values are
-- written by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked kind of employer` IS A `Kind of employer`
ASSUME `an unasked year` IS A `My year as a local nongroup employer`
ASSUME `an unasked group year` IS A `My group's year`
ASSUME `an unasked month` IS A `My month`

`as the employer` MEANS `I employ people, or pay directors, through my business (an employer)`
`as the agent` MEANS `I place workers with clients and pay them (an employment agent)`

`local nongroup` MEANS `a local nongroup employer: not in a group, and paying taxable wages only in WA`
`interstate nongroup` MEANS `an interstate nongroup employer: not in a group, and paying taxable wages in WA and in another State or Territory`
`group member` MEANS `a member of a group of employers under Part 4`

