§§ `For every employer: wages and WA taxable wages`

-- d044: a month's salary ($7,000) and the super on it ($840) are wages; so are director's fees. A freelance invoice is not
-- (finding 2); a boat builder's labour contract is, to its labour less GST ($40,000); a fixed-fee contract is not; a car
-- taxable for FBT is ($3,000), an exempt benefit is not; an agent's payment to a placed worker is ($10,000).
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` EQUALS amount 7000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `d044: the employer's super contribution for that month` EQUALS amount 840
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `director's fees Jarrah pays Daniel` EQUALS amount 5000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `a boat builder's labour contract, with GST` EQUALS amount 40000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `a boat builder's fixed-fee contract for a given result` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `a car provided to an employee, taxable for FBT` EQUALS amount 3000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `an exempt benefit under the FBTA Act` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `Jarrah as employment agent pays a placed worker` EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the agent` `Jarrah as employment agent pays a placed worker` EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` EQUALS amount (`How much of this payment is wages` `d044: a month's salary to an employee`)
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `a boat builder's labour contract, with GST` EQUALS amount (`How much of this payment is wages` `a boat builder's labour contract, with GST`)
#ASSERT `How much of this payment counts as wages` `as the employer` `a car provided to an employee, taxable for FBT` EQUALS amount (`How much of this payment is wages` `a car provided to an employee, taxable for FBT`)
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages for payroll tax` `as the employer` `an invoice from a freelance developer` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages for payroll tax` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages for payroll tax` `as the agent` `Jarrah as employment agent pays a placed worker` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages for payroll tax` `as the employer` `a boat builder's fixed-fee contract for a given result` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this payment wages for payroll tax` `as the employer` `an invoice from a freelance developer` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this payment wages` `an invoice from a freelance developer`)
-- s 6A: work wholly in Perth, yes; across WA and NSW by a Perth resident, yes, by a Sydney resident, no; a worker living
-- abroad, for a WA employer, yes; work wholly in London paid in Perth, yes.
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work across WA and NSW by a Perth resident` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work across WA and Singapore by a worker living abroad` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work wholly in London paid into a Perth account` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the agent` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Are these wages taxable in WA` `as the employer` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident` EQUALS `yes if` (`Are the wages taxable in WA` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident`)
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages, as I ask it` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS amount 7000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages, as I ask it` `as the employer` `parental leave pay exempt under Part 5` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages, as I ask it` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` `work across WA and NSW by a Sydney resident` EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages, as I ask it` `as the agent` `Jarrah as employment agent pays a placed worker` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `How much of this payment is WA taxable wages, as I ask it` `as the employer` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` `work done wholly in Perth` EQUALS amount (`How much of this payment is WA taxable wages` `d044: a month's salary to an employee` `work done wholly in Perth`)

§§ `For every employer: groups`

-- s 33: 60% of a partnership's profits is a controlling interest; exactly 50% is not.
#ASSERT `Does this person hold a controlling interest in the business` `as the employer` `60% of a partnership's profits` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this person hold a controlling interest in the business` `as the employer` `exactly 50% of a partnership's capital and profits` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this person hold a controlling interest in the business` `as the agent` `60% of a partnership's profits` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this person hold a controlling interest in the business` `as the employer` `exactly 50% of a partnership's capital and profits` EQUALS `yes if` (`Does the person hold a controlling interest` `exactly 50% of a partnership's capital and profits`)
-- ss 30-33, 38: Jarrah and Daniel's practice, grouped; a company he holds 40% of, not; the practice after the
-- Commissioner excludes Jarrah, not; a related body corporate cannot be excluded, grouped; a shared employee, grouped.
#ASSERT `Is my business grouped with the other business` `as the employer` `Jarrah and Daniel's consulting practice` EQUALS yes
